        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: புல்லாங்குழல்",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "புல்லாங்குழல் — pullāṅkuḻal — \"a flute\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "இடையன் மரத்தடியில் புல்லாங்குழல் ஊதினான். iṭaiyaṉ marattaṭiyil pullāṅkuḻal ūtiṉāṉ. The herdsman played the flute under a tree."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A flute is blown, so it takes ஊது (ūtu): புல்லாங்குழல் (pullāṅkuḻal) ஊது."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "புல்லாங்குழல் (pullāṅkuḻal) ends in the native குழல் (kuḻal), \"a tube, a flute, a pipe\" (DEDR 1818); the origin of the first part is not settled."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
